# apps/mobile publishes EXACTLY ONE variable, and this is the whole file.
#
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_` is not a namespace, it is a publication decision: babel-preset-expo INLINES the
# value into the JS bundle at build time, and the bundle ships inside the .ipa/.apk. Anyone who
# downloads the app can read every value under this prefix. There is therefore no provider
# credential here, no internal HMAC signing key, and no FastAPI hostname — this app talks to
# Laravel and only to Laravel (kb-architecture-map NN1), and a device that could sign an internal
# request would be a per-device copy of a service credential.
#
# The allow-list in app.config.ts fails the build on ANY other EXPO_PUBLIC_* key, including one
# added by accident and including the documented opt-out flag that would restore Hermes'
# XHR-backed fetch and make `Response.body` null — which is how a streaming chat silently stops
# streaming while every test still passes. That flag is not named anywhere in this directory,
# deliberately: CI greps for it, and a comment explaining the grep would fail the grep.
#
# Origin only: scheme + host + optional port. No path, no trailing slash — src/api/client.ts
# concatenates a leading-slash path onto it, and a trailing slash produces `//api/v1/...`, which
# some proxies normalise and some route to a 404.
#
# In a build, this value comes from the matching `env` block in eas.json, not from a .env file.
# This example documents the local `expo start` case.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8080
